# Testing standards

- `pytest` + `pytest-asyncio`. Never call a real model or Higgsfield API in a test —
  record/replay a cassette or stub the gateway/provider abstraction.
- Every node with a QC/repair or retry loop needs a test per terminal state: `SUCCESS`,
  `PARTIAL`, `FAILED_NO_PROGRESS`, `FAILED`/`ESCALATED` — don't only test the happy path.
- Test checkpoint/resume explicitly: kill a run mid-graph in the test and assert it resumes
  from the last checkpoint rather than restarting finished work.
- Test idempotency: issue the same request twice with the same `Idempotency-Key` and assert
  no duplicate work or billing.
- Anything touching cost or prompts needs a benchmark test — CI blocks merges on >3% eval
  regression or >20% cost regression, so a change with no such test can't be evaluated by
  that gate.
